  "reviewConclusions": [
    "The defect is the legacy synthetic replay losing the separately approved current-target request. The native M2 standardCourse must remain native; the M3 operating target is a distinct exact application.",
    "Assigning the issued proof to reproduced is safe only after the existing strict validator returns true: that validator independently reconstructs the full proof from the exact original request and compares it with this receipt, including renderer seal and current ACTIVE registry.",
    "The new branch does not grant renderer continuity by key presence. Wrong schema, missing/changed typed sidecar, source drift, changed approvals, replay-before mismatch, or renderer seal failure still reject.",
    "The existing post-validation previous-payload allowlist is still mandatory. The imported validator does not replace that renderer obligation.",
    "The exact helper still preserves native original curriculum UNSPECIFIED, null 2015 exact RPM leaf, unresolved 2022 binding, and no full semantic/math/source-quality approval."
  ],
